<title>GERMANY: Jochimsen cautious on EMU stability council idea.</title>
<headline>Jochimsen cautious on EMU stability council idea.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Reimut Jochimsen said on Friday that he was concerned that proposals for a stability council to monitor the euro currency after the 1999 EMU start could endanger the independence of the European Central Bank (ECB).</p>
<p>In the text of a speech delivered in Luxembourg but made available here in advance, Jochimsen said it was important to establish that the ECB would really be able to make its decisions independently of political influence.</p>
<p>&quot;Therefore a high degree of caution is required with regard to the setting up of a so-called &quot;stability council&quot; as has been mainly suggested by the French side,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
